Package: dvbtx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: BILLY Rémi <byhoster.association@gmail.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), ffmpeg, tzdata, @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: tsduck, hackrf, uhd-host, streamlink, yt-dlp, dvb-tools
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/TrusterBSW/DVB-Tx
Description: home DVB-T transmitter for a closed coax network (HackRF, USRP, SoapySDR)
 dvbtx builds complete DVB multiplexes from live streams (HLS, RTMP, SRT, Twitch,
 M3U, tvheadend), capture devices (webcam, HDMI capture, screen), files and pipes,
 and modulates them on a software radio: any number of DVB-T carriers per radio,
 any number of radios and services, configured in one TOML file or on the command
 line.
 .
 The C engine multiplexes on the modulator clock (exact rate, PCR restamped,
 automatic switch to a backup clip), builds PSI/SI (NIT with logical channel
 numbers, SDT, EIT from XMLTV, TOT) and synthesises all the OFDM carriers of a
 radio in one FFT. A web page shows the bit rates, the decoding margin of every
 service and the alerts; the TSDuck analysis can be exported as JSON.
 .
 Radiating on broadcast frequencies is forbidden: closed coax only.
